/**
 * VibeGrid CSS - Pure CSS Responsive Solution
 * 
 * 🎯 THE HOLY GRAIL: CSS max() function handles expand-vs-scroll automatically
 * ✅ No JavaScript width calculations needed
 * ✅ No ResizeObserver complexity
 * ✅ No magic number hacks
 * ✅ Works perfectly with your existing layout system
 */

/* ============================================================================
   CRITICAL: Force Container Width Constraints - The Table Scrolling Solution
   ============================================================================ */

/* 
   THE PROBLEM:
   - Tables have extremely strong intrinsic sizing behavior
   - When a table has fixed column widths (table-layout: fixed), it calculates
     its natural width and forces ALL parent containers to expand to fit
   - This breaks horizontal scrolling because containers grow instead of
     allowing the table to overflow
   - Normal CSS approaches (max-width: 100%, contain: layout, etc.) don't work
     because table sizing behavior overrides them

   THE SOLUTION: width: 0 + min-width: 100% trick
   - width: 0 tells the browser "don't let my content affect parent sizing"
   - min-width: 100% says "but fill my parent's available space"  
   - This breaks the connection between table width and container width
   - Containers are sized by their PARENT'S available space, not their content
   - Works with any sidebar state because it adapts to actual available space
*/

.vibegrid-container {
  /* 🎯 CRITICAL: width: 0 prevents content from affecting parent container sizing */
  width: 0;
  /* 📏 Fill parent's actual available space (adapts to sidebar state) */
  min-width: 100%;
  max-width: 100%;
  
  /* Use flexbox to control child sizing predictably */
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  
  /* Prevent any expansion beyond available layout space */
  overflow: hidden;
}

/* Table container - the border/background wrapper */
.vibegrid-container > div {
  /* 🎯 INHERIT: Same sizing technique as parent */
  width: 0;           /* Don't affect parent sizing */
  min-width: 100%;    /* Fill parent's available space */
  max-width: 100%;    /* Never exceed parent */
  
  /* Flex item that adapts to parent constraints */
  flex-shrink: 1;
  
  /* Prevent overflow - let child handle scrolling */
  overflow: hidden;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

/* ============================================================================
   Table Wrapper - The Horizontal Scrolling Container
   ============================================================================ */

.vibe-grid-table-wrapper {
  /* 🎯 FINAL CONTAINER: Constrained to actual layout space, not table content */
  width: 0;           /* Table width won't affect this container */
  min-width: 100%;    /* Use all available space from parent */
  max-width: 100%;    /* Never exceed available space */
  
  /* 📜 ENABLE SCROLLING: Now that container is properly constrained */
  overflow-x: auto;
  overflow-y: visible;
  
  /* Flex behavior */
  flex-shrink: 1;     /* Can shrink if needed */
  
  /* Enhanced scrolling experience */
  scroll-behavior: smooth;
  -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
  
  /* Allow cell editing overlays to extend beyond wrapper */
  position: relative;
  z-index: 1;
  
  /* Ensure proper box model */
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

/* 
   HOW IT WORKS:
   1. Parent layout (sidebar + main area) determines available space
   2. vibegrid-container: width: 0 + min-width: 100% = fills available space
   3. Border wrapper: inherits constraints from parent
   4. Scroll wrapper: constrained to available space, NOT table content
   5. Table: 1308px width can now overflow the constrained wrapper
   6. Result: Horizontal scrollbar appears!

   RESPONSIVE BEHAVIOR:
   - Sidebar collapsed (more space): containers expand, less scrolling needed
   - Sidebar expanded (less space): containers shrink, more scrolling needed
   - Works with any sidebar width without hardcoded values
*/

/* ============================================================================
   Main Table - Calculated Width for Horizontal Scrolling
   ============================================================================ */

.vibe-grid-table {
  /* 🎯 CRITICAL FIX: Calculate width from column sizes, allow overflow */
  width: auto;
  
  /* Essential for fixed column widths */
  table-layout: fixed;
  border-collapse: collapse;
}

/* When table has fixed column widths, ensure it sizes properly */
.vibe-grid-table th,
.vibe-grid-table td {
  /* Let column widths be controlled by inline styles */
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

/* Alternative approach for better browser support */
@supports not (width: fit-content) {
  .vibe-grid-table {
    /* Fallback: Set specific width based on column sizes */
    width: auto;
  }
}

/* ============================================================================
   Virtual Scrolling Containers
   ============================================================================ */

.vibe-grid-virtual-container {
  /* Enable horizontal scrolling for virtual tables */
  overflow-x: auto;
  width: 100%;
  
  /* Smooth scrolling */
  scroll-behavior: smooth;
  -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
}

.vibe-grid-header-row {
  /* Header row uses the same magic width calculation */
  width: max(100%, min-content);
  display: flex;
  
  /* Ensure header doesn't shrink */
  flex-shrink: 0;
}

.vibe-grid-virtual-body {
  /* Virtual body container */
  position: relative;
  
  /* Each virtual row will use the same width calculation */
  width: max(100%, min-content);
}

/* ============================================================================
   Pure CSS max() Solution - No JavaScript needed
   ============================================================================ */

/* The max() function automatically handles all responsive behavior:
 * - Expands to fill container when space is available
 * - Enables horizontal scrolling when content exceeds container
 * - No ResizeObserver, timeouts, or JavaScript measurements needed
 */

/* ============================================================================
   Responsive Behavior Explanation
   ============================================================================ */

/*
  How the max() function works:

  1. When container is WIDER than table content:
     - 100% (e.g., 2000px) > min-content (e.g., 1300px)
     - max() resolves to 100% (2000px)
     - Table expands to fill container
     - No horizontal scrolling

  2. When container is NARROWER than table content:
     - 100% (e.g., 800px) < min-content (1300px)
     - max() resolves to min-content (1300px)
     - Table maintains its natural width
     - overflow-x: auto activates horizontal scrolling

  3. During sidebar transitions:
     - CSS recalculates max() automatically on every frame
     - No JavaScript coordination needed
     - Smooth transitions without stepping effects
     - No timing issues or magic number corrections

  PROBLEM: If this isn't working, it means:
  - The wrapper isn't constraining the table properly
  - The table's min-content isn't being calculated correctly
  - There are conflicting CSS rules
  - Browser doesn't support max() with min-content properly
*/